From 3d7395317f223a4697f5c3eb260fbc1b726a5aa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:56:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Agent: recreate VLAN subinterfaces on VID change instead of
 in-place retag

Change the VID-only traffic separation config-change path in
TrunkPortPlumbing8021q from an in-place retag to a destroy+recreate of
only the affected subinterface(s). Previously, when a private/guest
VLAN ID changed but the bridges/trunk-set stayed the same, the existing
VLAN subinterface was retagged in place (kernel VLAN ID changed via
set_vlan_interface_id(), then renamed via rename_interface()) without
detaching it from its bridge, to avoid an STP re-convergence. This is
replaced with an explicit remove-from-bridge, delete, create new VLAN
subinterface with the new VID, and re-add to the same bridge -
mirroring the create path already used when subinterfaces are built
from scratch, but scoped to just the subinterface(s) whose VID
actually changed. Private and guest roles are evaluated and touched
independently, so if only one VID changes, the other subinterface is
left completely untouched. This intentionally re-triggers STP on the
affected bridge port; that trade-off is accepted in favor of always
ending up with a subinterface name/VID pair that is verifiably
consistent, rather than a partially-applied in-place retag.
retag_subifaces() is renamed to recreate_changed_subifaces() so its
name matches its new behaviour.

network_utils::set_vlan_interface_id() and rename_interface() are
removed - both were introduced only for the in-place retag and have no
remaining callers.

Signed-off-by: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
